# Reply to Comments on the Loanable-Funds Approach to Teaching Macroeconomics.

**Authors:** Fleisher, Belton M., Kopecky, Kenneth J.

## Abstract
Addresses three points Mark A. Nadler made in his analysis of the authors' paper, &quot;Loanable-funds Approach to Teaching Macroeconomics.&quot; Argues that Nadler's questions relate to intermediate or advanced analysis of macroeconomics, concluding that the loanable-funds approach is an appropriate elementary macro model. (LS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ398295

